  "label": "Racialized Assumption About Family Structure",
  "description": "The meme assumes that calling a non-biological man 'daddy' is inherently problematic or confusing, and this assumption is implicitly tied to racialized narratives that portray Black families as less conventional or more prone to confusion in familial roles. This is a form of racial stereotyping that frames non-traditional family structures as inherently unstable or morally ambiguous.",
